From 00ed947b4fec962d69c4593b27f91f2e642a4701 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:17:05 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Detect Fabric, Quilt and Forge projects and run them in
 rules-only mode

- ProjectAnalyzer detects NeoForge, Forge, Fabric and Quilt from metadata
  files, falling back to Gradle markers. Multi-loader projects are
  reported as unknown instead of being guessed; legacy NeoForge projects
  that still use META-INF/mods.toml are told apart from Forge by Gradle.
- MigrationEngine no longer rejects non-NeoForge projects. NeoForge keeps
  the full pipeline; other loaders copy the project, apply the rules of
  their loader and update only gradle.properties keys that already exist.
  Unknown loader versions are left untouched and reported, never invented.
- --neoforge-version is rejected for other loaders; --template must use
  the same loader as the source.
- Rules accept loader "*" to apply to every loader.
- Version profiles accept an optional "properties" map for extra
  gradle.properties entries; CLI and GUI profile listings are
  loader-neutral.
- Add LoaderSupportTest and document loader support and its limits.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017cjHkPet6EQbigJBGtkEKc
---
